      "trackId": "gemma4-e2b-iphone-mlx-v1",
      "description": "Gemma 4 E2B MLX Swift inference speedup track for iPhone 16 Pro Max (A18 Pro, 8 GB), macOS-verified. Target: mlx-community/gemma-4-E2B-it-qat-4bit @ 42f62737af7a9fd8c1d55d79666c1a217be4e2e2 -- a 35-layer text decoder (4:1 sliding_attention:full_attention hybrid, sliding window 512, shared K/V on the last 20 layers, PLE per-layer embeddings, hidden 1536, 8 heads over 1 KV head, tied embeddings, 262144-token vocab) with vision and audio towers in the checkpoint; the audio tower is NOT yet loadable by mlx-swift-lm and its weights are skipped at load. The paired MTP drafter (mlx-community/gemma-4-E2B-it-qat-assistant-4bit @ 7acb8d02364777be103dbf8c8dcb007f55f717e6) is a 4-layer shared-KV assistant that drafts blockSize-1 tokens per round; the candidate arm runs it at draft depth 3. Score = composite = prefill_gain^0.25 * decode_gain^0.75 against the same build's serial control legs, clamped per-gain to [0.95, 5.0]. A run is refused unless serial and candidate outputs match exactly, neither is degenerate (empty or all-<pad>), and the teacher-forced golden matches at rate >= 0.95. Optimize Sources/PhoneFastModel (loader, forward orchestration, cache/draft policy), Runner/E2B, and the vendored MLX/Metal kernel families the forward dispatches. Target quantization is frozen as shipped (4-bit affine, group 64, MLP projections at 8 bits).",
